.TH TDE\-AI\-CLIENT 1 "November 2026" "tde-ai-client 0.1.0" "Trinity Desktop Environment"
.SH NAME
tde\-ai\-client \- chat with AI services on the Trinity Desktop
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tde\-ai\-client
.RB [ \-b | \-\-backend
.IR service ]
.RB [ \-m | \-\-mode
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-p | \-\-prompt
.IR text ]
.RI [ file ...]
.RI [ "generic TDE options" ]
.RI [ "generic TQt options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tde\-ai\-client
(TDE AI Client) is a native application for the Trinity Desktop Environment
(TDE) for working with AI language and image models. It connects to
.IP \(bu 2
the
.BR "AI Horde" ,
a free, volunteer run service (https://aihorde.net) that needs no account;
.IP \(bu 2
.BR KoboldCpp
running on the same computer or in the local network;
.IP \(bu 2
any service with an
.BR "OpenAI\-compatible API" ,
such as OpenAI, OpenRouter, Mistral, Groq, Ollama, llama.cpp or LocalAI.
.PP
Besides chatting, it can have images generated and text read aloud where the
service offers that. Files can be attached to messages: text files are sent
with every service; images, audio, video and other files are sent to
services and models that can handle them. Conversations are saved
automatically and can be exported as web pages or plain text.
.PP
Everything typed and attached is sent to the selected service. With the AI
Horde and with cloud services that is a computer run by someone else.
.PP
The complete documentation is available as the
.I TDE AI Client Handbook
in the TDE Help Center
.RB ( "khelpcenter help:/tde\-ai\-client" ),
or by pressing F1 in the application.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-backend " \fIservice\fR"
Select the service to use:
.BR horde ,
.B koboldcpp
or
.BR openai .
Without this option the service used last is selected.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " \fImode\fR"
Select what the service should do:
.B chat
(the default),
.B image
(generate an image from the text) or
.B speech
(read the text aloud). If the service does not offer the mode, nothing is
sent.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prompt " \fItext\fR"
Send
.I text
as soon as the program has started, together with the files given.
.TP
.I file
One or more files to attach to the first message.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the options, including the generic TDE and TQt options.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information.
.SH EXAMPLES
Ask the AI Horde a question:
.PP
.RS
.B tde\-ai\-client \-\-backend horde \-\-prompt \(dqWhat is the Trinity Desktop?\(dq
.RE
.PP
Have a KoboldCpp server with a vision model describe a picture:
.PP
.RS
.B tde\-ai\-client \-b koboldcpp \-p \(dqWhat is this?\(dq photo.jpg
.RE
.PP
Generate an image:
.PP
.RS
.B tde\-ai\-client \-b horde \-m image \-p \(dqa lighthouse at sunset, oil painting\(dq
.RE
.PP
Start with a source file attached and type the question in the window:
.PP
.RS
.B tde\-ai\-client main.cpp
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $TDEHOME/share/config/tde\-ai\-clientrc
Settings: service addresses, API keys (unless they are kept in TDEWallet),
generation parameters and the models chosen last. Readable by the owner
only.
.TP
.I $TDEHOME/share/apps/tde\-ai\-client/conversations/
The saved conversations, one JSON file each.
.TP
.I $TDEHOME/share/apps/tde\-ai\-client/media/
Images and audio received from services, and images pasted from the
clipboard.
.PP
.B TDEHOME
defaults to
.IR ~/.trinity .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TDEHOME
The directory holding the user's TDE settings and data.
.PP
Network access goes through the TDE I/O framework: proxy settings are those
configured in the TDE Control Centre.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/Yjlion/tde\-ai\-client/issues.
